    "reply": "I reviewed `shop/payments.py` and wrote the findings to `/tmp/skilldiff-jd13l_40/ws/REVIEW.md`. The verdict is **REQUEST CHANGES**.\n\nThe main problem is that money is handled as floats. `TAX_RATE` is a float, and `line_total`, `order_total` and `refund` all do float arithmetic. `order_total` also uses `round()`, which is unreliable for currency. The file needs `Decimal` with explicit `ROUND_HALF_UP` quantization.\n\nThere are also no tests. The repo has no `tests/` directory and nothing references `payments`. `refund` has no validation, so it accepts negative amounts or amounts above the order total.\n\nI did not modify any source files.",
